 "description": "A talking (or singing) character from one image and a voice track (InfiniteTalk on Wan 2.1): lips, head and body move with the audio. One speaker per clip; for a dialogue, make a clip per line and cut them together (video.compose). Use it for story scenes, trailers and Imagine Live TV dialogue. Pair with audio.voice for the line. The clip is two passes of frames each, joined without the frames the second pass repeats (2 x frames - 9: 6.1 s at the defaults) whatever the audio length; size frames to the line and trim the rest in the cut. v3 drops those repeated frames (v2 kept them, so everything in the second pass ran 0.36 s behind the voice). v1 rendered black frames: its two-speaker masks were empty.",
